[{"id":"ceq-fill","itemId":"case-equality","role":"core","promptHtml":"Type the comparison that counts an X on <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> as a difference from <code class=\"nobreak\">d_at_edge</code>.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">!==</code> treats X as a value of its own, so <code>q !== d_at_edge</code> is 1 when <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> is X and <code class=\"nobreak\">d_at_edge</code> is not, and the check fails as it should (lesson 3.3). With <code class=\"nobreak\">!=</code> the condition would be X, the <code class=\"nobreak\">if</code> would not run its lines, and the X would pass unnoticed.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-02/dff/dff_tb.sv","firstLine":18,"totalLines":68,"before":["  // What a D flip-flop must do: remember d at each rising edge.","  always @(posedge clk) d_at_edge <= d;","","  // Wait for the next falling edge, check q, then set d for the next cycle.","  // Changing d on falling edges keeps it steady at every rising edge.","  task automatic next_cycle(input logic value);","    @(negedge clk);"],"blankLine":{"left":"    if (q ","right":" d_at_edge) begin"},"after":["      $display(\"TEST FAILED: q=%b, expected %b at %0d ns\",","               q, d_at_edge, $time);","      errors = errors + 1;","    end","    d = value;","  endtask"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// What a D flip-flop must do: remember d at each rising edge.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) d_at_edge ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// Wait for the next falling edge, check q, then set d for the next cycle.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// Changing d on falling edges keeps it steady at every rising edge.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"task","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"automatic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"next_cycle","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" value);","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"negedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk);","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":" d_at_edge) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]},"after":[[{"text":"      ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"$display","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"\"TEST FAILED: q=","color":"var(--code-token-string-expression)","bold":false},{"text":"%b","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":", expected ","color":"var(--code-token-string-expression)","bold":false},{"text":"%b","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":" at ","color":"var(--code-token-string-expression)","bold":false},{"text":"%0d","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":" ns\"","color":"var(--code-token-string-expression)","bold":false},{"text":",","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"               q, d_at_edge, ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"$time","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"      errors ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" errors ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"+","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    d ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" value;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"endtask","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["!=="],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The missing operator"},{"id":"ceq-predict-loose","itemId":"case-equality","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"This is the testbench of a 4-bit register with a bug. <code class=\"nobreak\">expected</code> is its model, and <code class=\"nobreak\">loose</code> is <code>q != expected</code>: the comparison without the second <code class=\"nobreak\">=</code>. <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">expected</code> are drawn in hexadecimal, and a bus with any X bit is drawn as X; where <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> is drawn as X here, its other bits equal <code class=\"nobreak\">expected</code>'s. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">loose</code> for each cycle: 0, 1 or X.","explanationHtml":"<p>In cycles 0 and 1, <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> has X bits and its other bits match <code class=\"nobreak\">expected</code>, so <code class=\"nobreak\">!=</code> cannot say whether they differ: <code class=\"nobreak\">loose</code> is X (lesson 3.3). Where <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">expected</code> hold the same value it is 0. In cycle 6 <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> is C and <code class=\"nobreak\">expected</code> is 0, so it is 1. The testbench's real check, <code class=\"nobreak\">!==</code>, is 1 in cycles 0 and 1 as well. A check written with <code class=\"nobreak\">!=</code> would not run its lines there, and would miss two of the three failures.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"reg4-loose","source":"hdl/level-03/reg4_bug/reg4_bug_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"reg4_bug_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"rst","path":"reg4_bug_tb.rst","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[3.5,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5.5,"1"],[6.5,"0"]]},{"label":"q[3:0]","path":"reg4_bug_tb.q","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"xx00"],[2,"1010"],[3,"0011"],[4,"0000"],[5,"1100"],[7,"0101"]]},{"label":"expected[3:0]","path":"reg4_bug_tb.expected","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0000"],[2,"1010"],[3,"0011"],[4,"0000"],[5,"1100"],[6,"0000"],[7,"0101"]]},{"label":"loose","path":"reg4_bug_tb.loose","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"x"],[2,"0"],[6,"1"],[7,"0"]],"samples":["x","x","0","0","0","0","1","0"],"allowX":true}]},"answer":"loose"},{"id":"ceq-choice-missed","itemId":"case-equality","role":"core","promptHtml":"In a testbench, <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> is X and <code class=\"nobreak\">expected</code> is 0. The check is written with <code class=\"nobreak\">!=</code> where the course writes <code class=\"nobreak\">!==</code>: if <code>q != expected</code>, it prints TEST FAILED and adds 1 to <code class=\"nobreak\">errors</code>. What does <code>q != expected</code> give, and what happens?","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">!=</code> cannot say whether an X differs from 0, so it gives X, and an <code class=\"nobreak\">if</code> whose condition is X does not run its lines: nothing is printed or counted, and the bug walks past (lesson 3.3). The comparison itself gives X, not 0, and an X stops nothing: the simulation runs on. With <code class=\"nobreak\">!==</code> the condition is 1 and the check fails as it should.</p>","type":"choice","options":["X, so the `if` does not run its lines: the difference is not counted","1, so the `if` runs its lines: the difference is counted","0, because an X counts as 0: there is no difference to count","X, so the simulation stops with an error"],"correct":0},{"id":"ceq-predict-alert","itemId":"case-equality","role":"core","promptHtml":"This is lesson 0.2's alarm: <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is <code>armed &amp; opening</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> is <code>door_open | window_open</code>. Wherever an input is drawn hatched, the testbench leaves it at X, as if nothing had set it. <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is not drawn. The testbench works out <code class=\"nobreak\">alert</code>, which is <code>siren !== 1'b0</code>. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">alert</code> for each step: 0, 1 or X.","explanationHtml":"<p>First work out <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> (lesson 3.2). An X decides nothing where another input already does: with <code class=\"nobreak\">armed</code> at 0, or with the door and the window both at 0, <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is 0 (steps 0, 3 and 6); a door or window at 1 makes <code class=\"nobreak\">opening</code> 1 even beside an X, so with <code class=\"nobreak\">armed</code> at 1 <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is 1 (steps 2 and 7). Everywhere else it is X (steps 1, 4 and 5). Then <code class=\"nobreak\">!==</code> treats X as a value of its own and gives 1 or 0, never X (lesson 3.3): X !== 0 is 1, and 1 !== 0 is 1. So <code class=\"nobreak\">alert</code> is 1 wherever <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is not a definite 0.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"alarm-x-alert","source":"hdl/level-03/alarm_x/alarm_x_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"armed","path":"alarm_x_tb.armed","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"x"],[2,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"x"],[5,"1"],[6,"0"],[7,"1"]]},{"label":"door_open","path":"alarm_x_tb.door_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"x"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"],[6,"1"]]},{"label":"window_open","path":"alarm_x_tb.window_open","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[2,"1"],[3,"x"],[4,"0"],[5,"x"]]},{"label":"alert","path":"alarm_x_tb.alert","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[6,"0"],[7,"1"]],"samples":["0","1","1","0","1","1","0","1"],"allowX":true}]},"answer":"alert"}]